---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
import { getVisibleGames, getVisiblePosts, gameUrl } from '../lib/games';

const games = await getVisibleGames();
const posts = await getVisiblePosts();
---

<PageLayout title="About" eyebrow="Who we are" description={`${SITE.name} is a tiny independent studio making small original games you can play free in your browser, with guides and devlogs for each.`}>
  <p class="lead">
    {SITE.name} is a tiny independent game studio. We make small, original games that you can play for free in your browser, on a computer or a phone,
    with no account and nothing to install.
  </p>

  <p>
    Every game on this site is made here: the design, the code, the levels and the chiptune music, and most of the pixel art. There are no asset
    flips and no copies of other people's games. When a game uses art we didn't draw ourselves, its page says so in the credits.
  </p>

  <h2>Our games</h2>
  <ul>
    {
      games.map((g) => (
        <li>
          <a href={gameUrl(g)}>
            <strong>{g.data.title}</strong>
          </a>
          : {g.data.shortDescription}
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>
  <p>
    Each game also has a free Android app with no ads and no in-app purchases. They're downloaded straight from this site; our guide on <a
      href="/blog/install-android-apk-safely/">installing them safely</a
    > explains how.
  </p>

  <h2>Why "INDIE/24"?</h2>
  <p>
    The name comes from the idea we started with: one game in the spotlight at a time, so it gets proper attention instead of being one tile in a
    wall of hundreds. The <strong>Game of the Day</strong> on the home page is always our newest release, and every game we've made stays in the <a
      href="/games/">archive</a
    >. We add new games as they're finished. Quality comes first, so we'd rather release a good game every week or two than a rushed one every day.
  </p>

  <h2>Guides and devlogs</h2>
  <p>
    We write about our games too: strategy guides and walkthroughs, written with the real numbers from each game's code, and devlogs about how each
    game was built, including what went wrong. There are {posts.length} posts so far in <a href="/blog/">Guides &amp; Devlog</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How we make games</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Play first.</strong> Every game runs in a browser and starts in a second or two. No sign-ups, no downloads, no loading screens.</li>
    <li><strong>Phones count.</strong> Every game works with touch, and every level is tested to be beatable with on-screen controls.</li>
    <li><strong>Fair, even when it's mean.</strong> Our games can be hard, but they're never random in a way that cheats you. We test them with programs that prove every level and every gap can be beaten.</li>
    <li><strong>Small and fast.</strong> Art is drawn with code and music is generated live, so a whole game is smaller than one photo.</li>
    <li><strong>Your data stays yours.</strong> Progress is saved on your device. The only thing we ever ask for is an optional nickname for the leaderboard. See our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Keeping the lights on</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is free to play. To pay for hosting and development, the website shows a small number of clearly marked ads <em>around</em> the
    pages. There are never ads inside the games themselves, and the Android apps have none at all.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Found a bug, got an idea for a game, or want to say hello? We'd love to hear from you on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. If something on
    the site looks wrong or unsafe, please use the <a href="/report/">Report a Game</a> page.
  </p>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
